  "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nIn Frankenstein, Mary Shelley shows that the creature becomes a monster because of how he is treated. When he is first created, the creature is gentle and wants to be loved. However, every person who sees him is scared of his appearance and attacks him or runs away. Even Victor Frankenstein, the man who made him, abandons him right after bringing him to life. The creature says, \"I was benevolent and good; misery made me a fiend.\" This line shows that his anger comes from being rejected over and over, not from his nature.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer wants to use the word \"isolation\" in this essay.\n\nWrite 5 different sentences that use \"isolation\" naturally and could fit into this paragraph, on its topic and in its argument. Each sentence must contain \"isolation\" (another form of the word, such as a plural or past tense, is fine). Use only ideas the paragraph already contains; do not invent statistics, names or quotations. Put the best sentences first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
